  "raw_text": "No. A filename alone cannot establish that two files are the same source-of-truth document, especially when they come from different folders or dates.\n\nYou would need additional evidence, such as:\n\n- File contents or cryptographic hashes\n- Version/revision identifiers\n- Creation and modification timestamps\n- Document metadata\n- Author or system-of-record information\n- Repository history, audit logs, or access controls\n- An approved document-management policy identifying the authoritative location\n\nIdentical filenames show only a naming match, not identity, version equivalence, or authority.",
